From b225c361406329212cc8410b07c6826def8b91ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:03:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/53] B70-IP-D2: native INT8 per-token-head KV decode on XPU
 FLASH_ATTN (B70_PTH_FA_DECODE=1)

What: with B70_PTH_FA_DECODE=1 (default off) FLASH_ATTN on XPU accepts
--kv-cache-dtype int8_per_token_head and decodes with the vllm-xpu-kernels
INT8 per-token-head paged decode (vllm-xpu-kernels, port of
wiesion's intel/llm-scaler#744).

1. Spec: FlashAttentionBackend.customize_spec packs int8_per_token_head like
   TRITON_ATTN (int8 K and V plus one fp32 scale each per token and KV head):
   same page bytes, so the hybrid page alignment, unify and B70-IP-K3 see the
   same pages as with TRITON_ATTN. Flag off: spec unchanged, dtype rejected.
2. Layout: the FA impl reads each of its blocks as the kernel's block-local
   split layout [int8 K|V (slot, head) | K scales | V scales] through views
   (b70_pth_fa.split_layout_views): K/V int8 [B, N, H, D] strides
   (page, H*2D, 2D, 1), V at +D, scales fp32 [B, N, H] strides (page/4, H, 1).
   Every K/V surface base is 64-byte aligned. A layer's pages are only touched
   by its own backend, so TRITON_ATTN (drafter) and QSA layers keep the inline
   layout; the QSA impl hands its parent "auto" and is unaffected. The views
   live in _k_scale_cache, which the runner clears after profiling.
3. Writer: TRITON_ATTN's per-token-head Triton writer through the split views
   (no SYCL writer exists for this layout); key/value cut to slot_mapping.
4. Decode: max q <= the kernels' _SPEC_DECODE_MAX_QLEN (16) and causal -> one
   flash_attn_varlen_func call with int8 K/V and the scale views as
   k_descale/v_descale (q 1: paged decode; q 2..16, ragged included: the
   kernels' per-position split-K route). Non-causal q <= 16 (DFlash draft
   blocks on FA): one decode row per query row, graph-safe.
5. Prefill / mixed / longer batches: K4's dequant-to-bf16 scratch + FA bf16,
   forced on (ignores B70_PTH_FA_PREFILL and B70_PTH_FA_MIN_Q), with the
   layer's causal flag, window and sinks. A full-graph capture of such a batch
   raises (it syncs with the host).
6. One-time log line "B70-IP-D2 int8_per_token_head KV on XPU FLASH_ATTN ...".

K4/K5 behaviour without the flag is unchanged (the stock K4 call passes the
same arguments; window/sinks stay None).

Measured: CPU tests only (next commit). No GPU, no boot.
